-- title:
--   Descent of fibrewise zero-locus containment along a field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $C$ a scheme, $c\colon C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ a morphism and $U$ an open subscheme of $C$; let $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ be a further morphism and $M$ a module on the fibre product $C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}R}T$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of that scheme has an open neighbourhood $V$ on which the restriction of $M$ along $V\hookrightarrow C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}R}T$ is isomorphic to the unit module of the sheaf of rings of $V$. Let $k$ be a field, $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to T$ a point, and $K$ a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure, giving the point $\operatorname{Spec}K\to\operatorname{Spec}k\xrightarrow{\,s\,}T$, where $\operatorname{Spec}K\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ is `Scheme.TwoAffineOpenCover.specMap k K`, the spectrum of the structure homomorphism $k\to K$. For a field-valued point $u$ of $T$ write $C_u=C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}R}\operatorname{Spec}(\cdot)$ for the pullback of $c$ along $u\circ$ followed by $t$ (formally $u\,\gg\!\!\gg t$), and let $M_u$ be the pullback of $M$ along `mapOnProdOver c u rfl`, the map $C_u\to C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}R}T$ induced by the identity of $C$ and $u$. For a morphism $\tau$ from the unit module to $M_u$, let $\operatorname{zeroSchemeIdeal}(\tau)$ be the infimum of all ideal sheaf data $J$ on $C_u$ such that, for every affine open $W$, the ideal of $J$ at $W$ contains the ideal generated by all coefficients of $\tau$ over $W$, and let its support be the associated closed subset. The hypothesis is that over the point $\operatorname{Spec}K\to T$ every nonzero such $\tau$ has $\operatorname{supp}\operatorname{zeroSchemeIdeal}(\tau)$ contained in the preimage of $U$ under the first projection; the conclusion is the same assertion over the point $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to T$.
--
--   This is a descent statement for the condition that the zero locus of every nonzero section of an invertible module on a fibre avoid the complement of $U$: it transfers the condition from the fibre over a field extension $K$ of the residue field of a point back to the fibre over that point, so that a condition verified at geometric points suffices at arbitrary field-valued points. It is used, alongside the corresponding descent of vanishing of Čech $H^1$, in the construction of charts for a relative Picard functor fibre by fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_RelPicard_support_zeroSchemeIdeal_fibre_subset_of_support_zeroSchemeIdeal_fibre_subset_extension.lean

